SOURCE-HEADER CHECK SCOPE
========================

scripts/check-license-headers.py checks supported first-party source and Makefiles
across the repository, including release/E2E scripts and source under docs/,
site/, and .github/ when present. scripts/add-license-headers.py offers a dry run and
requires explicit authorship confirmation before adding missing headers. Both
accept --root PATH for a checkout or source export. Existing notices and
unrecognized generated files require review rather than automatic replacement.

The named provenance exceptions above are encoded in scripts/license_headers.py.
Markdown, YAML, JSON, lockfiles, module manifests, binary assets, hidden paths
other than .github/, dependencies, and build outputs are not assigned comment
headers. Third-party and generated/scaffold exceptions retain their existing
notices and require provenance review. These scope boundaries are not exemptions
from their underlying licenses.

